.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Signal handling for the 42sh shell\&. 


.PP
\fBAuthor\fP
.RS 4
pulgamecanica 
.RE
.PP

.SH "Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "void signals_check (\fBt_shell\fP * shell)"

.PP
Process any pending signal that was caught during the last prompt\&. Called in the main loop before each prompt iteration\&.

.PP
Sets $? to the appropriate value (130 for SIGINT = 128 + 2)\&. 
.SS "void signals_setup_child (void )"

.PP
Restore default signal handlers in a child process before execve\&. After fork the child inherits the parent's signal dispositions (SIG_IGN for interactive mode)\&. We must reset them to SIG_DFL so the executed program responds to signals normally\&. 
.SS "void signals_setup_executing (void )"

.PP
Set up signal handlers for executing context (parent waiting for fg child)\&. SIGINT — ignored (let signal reach the child process)

.PP
SIGQUIT — ignored (let signal reach the child process)

.PP
SIGTSTP — ignored (let signal reach the child process)

.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
The parent simply waits; the child handles or dies from the signal\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void signals_setup_interactive (void )"

.PP
Set up signal handlers for interactive mode (at the prompt)\&. SIGINT - custom handler: newline + redisplay prompt (like bash)

.PP
SIGQUIT - ignored (Ctrl-\\ does nothing at prompt) (for now\&.\&.\&. I think)

.PP
SIGTSTP - ignored for now (Ctrl-Z does nothing at prompt, will handle fg/bg job control later) 
.SH "Variable Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "volatile sig_atomic_t g_signal_received\fR [extern]\fP"

.PP
Global signal flag (volatile for signal handler safety) 
.PP
.RS 4
Forward declaration to avoid circular dependency with \fB42sh\&.h\fP 
.RE
.PP

